{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01TNdG7DcqjXxxcWf6xrre1u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The 4 skipped tests are from `CommandInvoker.init()` failures in `generated_tests.zig` — these tests need the `tri` binary available to invoke commands as a subprocess. They skip when the binary isn't found. This is by design — they are integration tests that need the built binary, not unit tests. The `jit.zig` and `treesitter` skips are for JIT/tree-sitter libraries not available at test time.\n\nThese are not bugs — they're environment-dependent tests that correctly skip. Not worth fixing in this loop."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6573,"cache_read_input_tokens":111980,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6573,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"44d2ecaa-b17e-43c0-bdaa-9bdb8e6b7a9a","uuid":"ce6ee827-f1a1-4486-ada2-e931461c1f51"}
